Development Environment Setup

I installed VS Code and the C/C++ extension for C programming.
I also installed MinGW-w64 to use GCC as my C compiler.
Initially, the "gcc" command was not recognized in the terminal.
I fixed the problem by adding the MinGW "bin" folder to the system PATH.
After restarting VS Code, I checked the setup using "gcc --version".
The compiler version was displayed successfully, so I compiled "hello.c".
Finally, the program ran successfully and displayed “Hello, World!”.
